  "decision_conditions": [
    "The unauthorised adverts due to their size, placement and siting, extending beyond the designated fascia zone, result in a visually intrusive and incoherent form of development which has led to demonstrable harm to visual amenity and fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Enfield Town Conservation Area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 72(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990. The harm caused is not outweighed by any identified public benefits and therefore fails to accord with Section 12 and Section 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024; Policy HC1 of the London Plan 2021; Policy 37, 40, 41 and 44 of the DMD 2014; Policy 30 and 31 of the Core Strategy 2010; and Enfield Shopfronts and Associated Advertisements Supplementary Planning Guidance."
  ],
